WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:06.106
"The Side Effects of Quinine (Tonic Water)
to Boost GLP-1"

00:00:07.441 --> 00:00:08.876
In my last video,
I talked about how

00:00:08.876 --> 00:00:11.545
the quinine in a third
of a liter of tonic water

00:00:11.545 --> 00:00:15.716
can suppress appetite
and cause people to lose weight.

00:00:15.716 --> 00:00:19.152
But there are "risks
for the consumption of quinine."

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:21.054
Quinine is a drug

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:23.824
and may in fact be among
the most common causes

00:00:23.824 --> 00:00:27.194
of severe
drug-induced disorders.

00:00:27.194 --> 00:00:29.329
Just the levels of quinine
found in tonic water

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:31.031
may cause potentially fatal

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:34.935
immunologically-mediated
hypersensitivity reactions,

00:00:34.935 --> 00:00:37.371
basically
like allergic reactions,

00:00:37.371 --> 00:00:38.939
where it interacts
with antibodies

00:00:38.939 --> 00:00:41.074
to trigger autoimmune reactions

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:43.844
that can cause chills, fever,
a drop in blood pressure,

00:00:43.844 --> 00:00:46.580
painful bluish discoloration
of the hands and feet,

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:49.416
and clotting
within your blood vessels.

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:50.517
It can also chew up

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:52.886
your red blood cells,
leading to anemia.

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:55.589
Chew up your platelets, leading
to bleeding and bruising.

00:00:55.589 --> 00:00:57.257
And chew up
your white blood cells,

00:00:57.257 --> 00:00:58.926
leading to immune dysfunction.

00:00:58.926 --> 00:01:00.427
As well as
acute kidney injury,

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:03.063
the dissolution of your muscles,
liver toxicity, heart damage,

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:05.432
respiratory failure,
low blood sugars, blindness,

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:08.568
and toxic epidermal necrolysis,

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:11.805
which can manifest
as genital blistering,

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:16.410
sloughed penile erosion,
or an eroded scrotum.

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:19.479
Even minute exposure to quinine
in common beverages

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:21.581
can cause
severe adverse reactions

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:23.750
involving multiple
organ systems.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.719
So, the "moral of the story"

00:01:25.719 --> 00:01:28.455
is that a relaxing gin and tonic
may be the cause

00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:31.091
of life-threatening disease.

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:34.594
Now, these are rare,
idiosyncratic reactions.

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:37.197
Just because peanuts
can be life-threatening

00:01:37.197 --> 00:01:38.799
to someone with a peanut allergy

00:01:38.799 --> 00:01:41.601
doesn’t mean everybody
needs to avoid peanuts.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.904
But there are
non-hypersensitivity

00:01:43.904 --> 00:01:45.505
adverse effects, too.

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:49.042
For example, when quinine
isn’t eroding scrotums,

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:51.445
it may still be shrinking them.

00:01:51.445 --> 00:01:53.480
Researchers found quinine
so damaging

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:55.582
to the testicles of rats
that they suggested

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:59.519
that quinine should be explored
as male contraceptive.

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:03.256
Quinine is an extremely toxic
agent in overdose,

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:06.093
with vision loss
as a common outcome.

00:02:06.093 --> 00:02:09.096
The reason people may have
quinine pills around their house

00:02:09.096 --> 00:02:12.699
is that some people take them
for nocturnal leg cramps.

00:02:12.699 --> 00:02:14.735
The U.S. Food and Drug
Administration concluded

00:02:14.735 --> 00:02:17.871
that this was not safe;
so, it banned quinine’s use

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:20.407
for this purpose in both
over-the-counter preparations

00:02:20.407 --> 00:02:21.608
and even in prescriptions,

00:02:21.608 --> 00:02:23.543
after receiving
hundreds of reports

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:26.380
of serious adverse events
associated with quinine use,

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:28.715
including 93 deaths.

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:30.717
It’s still available
with a prescription

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:32.419
as a malaria drug, though,

00:02:32.419 --> 00:02:35.389
which doctors were
prescribing for leg cramps,

00:02:35.389 --> 00:02:37.591
skirting FDA recommendations,

00:02:37.591 --> 00:02:40.527
but given its rare but serious
allergic-type reactions,

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:42.929
and risk of OD’ing
on quinine pills,

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:45.499
that’s probably not a good idea.

00:02:45.499 --> 00:02:47.701
Thankfully,
following warnings by the FDA,

00:02:47.701 --> 00:02:49.536
the use of quinine
for treatment of muscle cramps

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:52.172
has dramatically declined.

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:53.607
Of course, even though
the FDA banned it

00:02:53.607 --> 00:02:55.142
from one aisle
of the drug store,

00:02:55.142 --> 00:02:57.477
it still may be available
in another,

00:02:57.477 --> 00:02:59.279
in the form of tonic water.

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:00.914
Yeah, but can
the lower levels of the drug

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:04.051
found in drinks
still cause problems?

00:03:04.051 --> 00:03:06.386
Yes, an overdose
can leave you blind,

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:08.922
affecting not only the retina
in the back of your eye

00:03:08.922 --> 00:03:12.159
but the iris in the front,
leading to oval pupils.

00:03:12.159 --> 00:03:14.027
How bizarre is that?

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:16.730
Okay, okay,
but what if you don’t overdose?

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:19.466
Can quinine
still affect your vision?

00:03:19.466 --> 00:03:20.767
Following the identification

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:23.503
by the Armed Forces
Institute of Pathology

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:29.009
of quinine in autopsy specimens
from military pilot fatalities,

00:03:29.009 --> 00:03:31.111
researchers had volunteers
drink tonic water

00:03:31.111 --> 00:03:34.481
for two weeks and were indeed
able to show some abnormalities.

00:03:34.481 --> 00:03:36.783
Even transient blurring
of vision

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:38.418
can be disastrous if experienced

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:41.788
by anyone operating
heavy machinery at high speeds.

00:03:41.788 --> 00:03:44.257
So, given the concern
that tonic water consumption

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:46.660
may have contributed
to aviation accidents,

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:48.695
the use of tonic water by pilots

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:51.865
is actually forbidden
three days before flying.

00:03:51.865 --> 00:03:53.600
I didn’t know that.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:56.002
So, how much is too much?

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:58.271
There was a case reported
of a 46-year-old man

00:03:58.271 --> 00:04:01.074
with increasing
visual deterioration

00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:03.944
and difficulty with
night driving over three months,

00:04:03.944 --> 00:04:05.278
during which
he had been drinking

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:07.714
a gallon of tonic water a day.

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:10.750
Okay, so, a gallon
may be too much.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:13.320
This person was drinking
a liter of tonic water

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:14.554
prior to the onset of his

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:17.758
"Quinine water-triggered
heart arrhythmia."

00:04:17.758 --> 00:04:20.694
His doctors suggest the public
is simply unaware of the risks

00:04:20.694 --> 00:04:23.897
associated with excessive
consumption of tonic water,

00:04:23.897 --> 00:04:27.634
but how many people are drinking
almost a quart a day?

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:31.471
The "no-untoward-effect"
level in humans

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:34.775
has been estimated to be
52.5 mg of quinine a day,

00:04:34.775 --> 00:04:38.278
which is about a two and a half
cups (590 ml) of tonic water.

00:04:38.278 --> 00:04:41.748
Based on ototoxicity,
damage to our hearing,

00:04:41.748 --> 00:04:43.116
maybe we shouldn’t
drink much more

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:46.219
than two cups (470 ml) a day,
but these levels are based on

00:04:46.219 --> 00:04:48.622
trying to extrapolate
from animal models.

00:04:48.622 --> 00:04:51.825
Since quinine was so commonly
prescribed to treat leg cramps,

00:04:51.825 --> 00:04:53.827
can’t we just look at large
populations of people

00:04:53.827 --> 00:04:56.229
and see if anything
bad happened?

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:57.664
Yes, indeed, we can,

00:04:57.664 --> 00:05:01.067
and those prescribed quinine
had a 27 percent increased risk

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:06.573
of acute kidney injury,
which is not as bad as death:

00:05:06.573 --> 00:05:09.042
"Association Between
Long-term Quinine Exposure

00:05:09.042 --> 00:05:10.877
and All-Cause Mortality."

00:05:10.877 --> 00:05:13.413
Following 175,000 people
for about six years,

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:15.182
researchers found
that those who were taking

00:05:15.182 --> 00:05:17.651
about 200 mg of quinine a day

00:05:17.651 --> 00:05:21.354
had a 25 percent
greater risk of dying.

00:05:21.354 --> 00:05:22.622
Those on around 300 mg

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:24.824
had an 83 percent
greater risk of dying,

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:26.126
and those on 400 mg or more

00:05:26.126 --> 00:05:29.029
appeared to double
their risk for death.

00:05:29.029 --> 00:05:34.267
So, I would recommend
staying away from quinine.

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:36.670
Although the FDA has determined
that carbonated beverages

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:40.373
may safely contain up to 83 mg
of quinine per liter,

00:05:40.373 --> 00:05:43.643
bottles of bubbly drinks usually
don’t say how much is in them,

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:45.512
and some popular brands
don’t even list it

00:05:45.512 --> 00:05:47.447
as an ingredient at all.

00:05:47.447 --> 00:05:50.350
How do you know if your drink
has quinine or not?

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:52.552
Hold it up to a black light,

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:55.121
and if it lights up
with an iridescent blue glow,

00:05:55.121 --> 00:05:58.525
well, quinine
is the secret ingredient

00:05:58.525 --> 00:06:01.228
for making
fluorescent Jell-O shots.

